          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em simplicial identities
            encode the relationships between the face and degeneracy maps in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial object
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            The
            %strong simplicial identities
            are the duals to the
            %em simplicial relations
            of coface and codegeneracy maps described at
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                  %mo ∈
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            with
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                face maps
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mo ∂
                        %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial_i : S_n \to S_{n-1}
                obtained by omitting the
                = succeed "th" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            %li
              %p
                degeneracy maps
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi s
                        %mi i
                      %mo :
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi S
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_i : S_n \to S_{n+1}
                obtained by repeating the
                = succeed "th" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
          #SimplicialIdentities.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong simplicial identities
              satisfied by face and degeneracy maps as above are (whenever these maps are composable as indicated):
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi i
                            %mo ∘
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi j
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo =
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mrow
                                %mi j
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo ∘
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi i
                          %mtd
                            %mtext if
                          %mtd
                            %mi i
                            %mo &lt;
                            %mi j
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi s
                              %mi i
                            %mo ∘
                            %msub
                              %mi s
                              %mi j
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mo =
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %msub
                              %mi s
                              %mi j
                            %mo ∘
                            %msub
                              %mi s
                              %mrow
                                %mi i
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                          %mtd
                            %mtext if
                          %mtd
                            %mi i
                            %mo &gt;
                            %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\partial_i
                    \\circ
                    \\partial_j
                    \\;=\;
                    \\partial_{j-1}
                    \\circ
                    \\partial_i
                    \&amp;
                    \\text{if}
                    \&amp;
                    i \lt j
                    \\\
                    s_i
                    \\circ
                    s_j
                    \\;=\;
                    s_j
                    \\circ
                    s_{i-1}
                    \&amp;
                    \\text{if}
                    \&amp;
                    i \gt j
                    }
            #eq:MixedSimplicialIdentities.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mphantom
                      %mi AAAAA
                    %msub
                      %mo ∂
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∘
                    %msub
                      %mi s
                      %mi j
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi s
                                %mrow
                                  %mi j
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                              %mo ∘
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mi i
                            %mtd
                              %mtext if
                            %mtd
                              %mi i
                              %mo &lt;
                              %mi j
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi id
                            %mtd
                              %mtext if
                            %mtd
                              %mi i
                              %mo ∈
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                              %mi j
                              %mo ,
                              %mi j
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %msub
                                %mi s
                                %mi j
                              %mo ∘
                              %msub
                                %mo ∂
                                %mrow
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo −
                                  %mn 1
                            %mtd
                              %mtext if
                            %mtd
                              %mi i
                              %mo &gt;
                              %mi j
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    {\phantom{AAAAA}}
                    \\partial_i
                    \\circ
                    s_j
                    \\;=\;
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    s_{j-1}
                    \\circ
                    \\partial_i
                    \&amp;
                    \\text{if}
                    \&amp;
                    i \lt j
                    \\\
                    id
                    \&amp;
                    \\text{if}
                    \&amp;
                    i \in \{j, j+1\}
                    \\\
                    s_j
                    \\circ
                    \\partial_{i-1}
                    \&amp;
                    \\text{if}
                    \&amp;
                    i \gt j+1
                    }
                    \\right.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GoerssJardine09"} Goerss &amp; Jardine 1999/2009, I.1. (1.3)
          %p
          #DegeneracyMapsAreSplitMono.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              The middle case in
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:MixedSimplicialIdentities"} (1)
              implies in particular that degeneracy maps are (
