          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#RelationToNilpotencyOfDifferentials Relation to nilpotency of differentials
          %p
            The simplicial identities of def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SimplicialIdentities"}
            can be understood as a non-abelian or “unstable” generalization of the identity
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo ∘
                  %mo ∂
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\partial \circ \partial = 0
          %p
            satisfied by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentials"} differentials
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            (in
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homological+algebra"} homological algebra
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}[S]
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+abelian+group"} simplicial abelian group
            obtained form
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            by forming degreewise the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} free abelian group
            on the set of
            = succeed "-simplices," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chains+on+a+simplicial+set"} chains on a simplicial set
          %p
            Then using these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+linear+combinations"} formal linear combinations
            we can sum up all the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            face maps
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mo ∂
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi S
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial_i : S_n \to S_{n-1}
            into a single map:
          #TheAlternatingFaceMapDifferential.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong alternating face map differential
              in degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              of the simplicial set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              is the linear map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo :
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi S
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
